    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** leading the charge at a strong 74.01 rating; facing Canning, he holds the highest raw projection, bolstered by a favorable SP xERA of 4.51 and his prime cleanup spot. Close behind, **Sam Antonacci** (66.39) and **Josh Jung** (66.28) anchor the core. **Sam Antonacci** benefits immensely from his leadoff designation and a solid 0.400 xwOBA, while **Josh Jung** capitalizes on the highest SP xERA matchup of the day (5.12) against Peralta, making him a primary target for counting stats. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.16) remains a reliable anchor in the two-hole, the team is counting on these three to drive the offensive floor given the relatively daunting SP assignments for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, both of whom are facing arms with sub-3.20 xERAs.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Nolan Schanuel** on the bench despite his respectable 51.09 score. While he presents a safer floor than **Jackson Merrill** (49.49), **Jackson Merrill** maintains a slight edge in high-upside opportunity, forcing **Nolan Schanuel** to the pine as the odd man out in a crowded middle-infield configuration. We are exercising caution with **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo**, both falling beneath the 40.0 efficiency floor; **Nasim Nunez** specifically faces a tough defensive environment against an elite catcher, and **Coby Mayo** is hampered by a bottom-third order placement against a sharp arm in Jax. With **Jorge Polanco** remaining on the IL, we are managing our remaining depth carefully to ensure we maximize game caps without sacrificing our scarcity-driven need for stolen base potential.",
